      <!-- Description: executive summary or first key takeaway only (no full HTML body).
           This keeps the RSS file small and avoids duplicate-content issues with Google. -->
      <description><![CDATA[
        India&#39;s indigenous air defense gets a major boost as Astra Microwave delivers the first Virupaksha AESA radar prototype hardware to DRDO for the Su-30MKI fleet.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The system is developed by LRDE under DRDO to replace the aging Russian N011M Bars radar on the IAF Su-30MKI fleet.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The radar features approximately 2,400 Gallium Nitride transmit-receive modules across a 950mm antenna array.
        [SPLIT]
